SUMMARY:Banned in Boston: Is Censorship Still Stifling Free Speech? (A Talk
 s for Better Living Event)
LOCATION:Boston Public Library\, 700 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA 02116
DESCRIPTION:Join us in partnership with the Citywide Friends of the Boston 
 Public Library for a timely and thought-provoking conversation featuring N
 ew York Law School Professor of Law Emerita Nadine Strossen and Harvard La
 w School Professor Randall Kennedy —two of America's foremost authoritie
 s on free expression and the First Amendment. After the hour-long main pro
 gram\, a book signing with both speakers will be facilitated by our local 
 independent bookstore partner for this program\, Trident Booksellers.\nhtt
 ps://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a9840d52dac6e0037237e4c\nFrom Pushpin B
 oston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
