BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1c408640fa3ca5a06ff2dacc53f785417e8c7060@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261004T001530Z
DTSTART:20261006T211500Z
DTEND:20261006T231500Z
SUMMARY:Knighthood and the Realities of War in Medieval Germany
LOCATION:MIT\, 70 MEMORIAL DR\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Military history as a subfield within medieval studies has suff
 ered considerably from the fact that both medieval authors and modern scho
 lars have seen warfare as a nasty element of the human experience\, that i
 s better condemned or even ignored than studied. As a consequence\, the ex
 amination of warfare is often treated as an adjunct to other areas of inqu
 iry\, with the result that many well-meaning historians continue to pass a
 long shibboleths long-since discarded by the relatively small number of sp
 ecialists in medieval military history. This is particularly true with reg
 ard to scholarship dealing with the German kingdom because very few non-Ge
 rman speaking historians do much work on Germany\, and German-speaking his
 torians\, with some notable exceptions\, particularly in Switzerland and A
 ustria\, have eschewed the study of military matters in the period since t
 he Second World War. One particularly important shibboleth\, which still p
 ermeates studies of the German kingdom\, is the notion that warfare was do
 minated by small numbers of warrior aristocrats who fought on horseback. I
 n this paper\, I will be addressing four major themes that are intended to
  illuminate the bankruptcy of this model. These are “knighthood” as a 
 problem of military history\, the reality of warfare in pre-crusade Europe
 \, the centrality of sieges and fortifications to warfare\, and finally th
 e implications of this third fact for our understanding of the scope and s
 cale of warfare\, and the concomitant nature of governmental organization.
 \nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/knighthood-and-the-realities-of-war-in-me
 dieval-germany\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/knighthood-and-the-realities-of-war-in-m
 edieval-germany
END:VEVENT
