DTSTAMP:20261004T001530Z
DTSTART:20261019T211500Z
DTEND:20261019T231500Z
SUMMARY:Undoing Gender in French Literature
LOCATION:MIT\, 160 MEMORIAL DR\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:The French modernist canon has been read has a key site for sex
 ual dissidence\, but what about gender? In this talk\, Mat Fournier presen
 ts his book\, Dysphoric Modernism\, and questions the entanglements of the
  modern gender binary with state power and colonial history. Through readi
 ngs of Gide\, Genet\, Colette\, and others\, Fournier explores how narrati
 ves of sexual dissidence both deconstruct and reinforce mutually exclusive
  definitions of masculinity and femininity and racial discriminations. In 
 this web of contradictions\, modern gender appears as inherently dysphoric
 \, imposing untenable positions and perpetuating systemic hierarchies. Ult
 imately\, tracking the dysphoria traversing modernist writings offers a pe
 rspective into gender’s complicity with historical and contemporary fasc
 isms\, and offers strategies of resistance.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/even
 t/undoing-gender-in-french-literature\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpi
 n.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/undoing-gender-in-french-literature
END:VEVENT
